    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate on July 16, 2026, the Austin Waves offense centers on the versatility of our middle infield and outfield core. **Jorge Polanco** holds a marginal efficiency score of 52.33; while he faces a formidable arm in Aaron Nola, **Jorge Polanco** retains value through his projected middle-of-the-order positioning. However, the scarcity of stolen bases remains our primary constraint. Consequently, we are prioritizing high-sprint-rate assets like **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** in deep-roster scenarios, as their ability to generate value on the basepaths outweighs the risk of facing elite rotations. **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** remain our primary levers for R and RBI production, with current park factors providing a slight tailwind to their adjusted efficiency scores, keeping them well within our \"Strong\" start threshold.\n\nOur bench strategy today is heavily dictated by availability, with **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** sidelined by an organizational day off. The most difficult exclusion was **Andy Pages**, who fell just short of the starting rotation due to an unfavorable platoon split against the opposing starter\u2019s profile, which suppressed his projected AVG. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our highest-ceiling catalyst, he remains locked in the IL slot, necessitating a rotation of **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to mitigate the production vacuum. We are closely monitoring the 31% rain risk surrounding **Jorge Polanco**\u2019s matchup; should that game trend toward a postponement, we are prepared to pivot to **Jacob Wilson** or **Coby Mayo** to ensure we do not forfeit daily game caps on empty slots.",
